course: dictionary
lesson: 198
title: Alabama: a state and a river
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Alabama starts with a capital letter, so it is a proper noun: it names one particular place. The dictionary gives two meanings. It is a state in the south-east of the United States, and it is also a river in that state.
explain: «In 1955 Rosa Parks refused to give up her bus seat in Alabama.» The sentence tells you where this happened, so Alabama here means the state. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a place, or about water? The clue words decide which meaning fits.
explain: You will often meet Alabama in history lessons about the civil rights movement. Segregation laws kept Black and white people apart on buses, in schools and in shops. The Montgomery bus boycott, which followed Rosa Parks' protest, helped to end these unfair laws.
fact: Alabama is a proper noun, so it always begins with a capital letter.
fact: Alabama is a state in the south-east of the United States, and its capital is Montgomery.
fact: The Alabama is also a river that flows through that state, so one word can name both a place and a river.
fact: In 1955 Rosa Parks refused to give up her bus seat in Alabama, and this helped start the Montgomery bus boycott.
fact: Segregation laws kept Black and white people apart on buses, in schools and in shops, and they were unfair.
exercise: «In 1955 Rosa Parks refused to give up her bus seat in Alabama.» In this sentence, Alabama means what? | A bus company | *A state in the south-east of the United States | A town in Canada | A kind of cotton
exercise: Which word is a proper noun, a name that starts with a capital letter? | bus | seat | *Alabama | boycott
exercise: «Its capital is Montgomery.» What is the capital of Alabama? | Glasgow | Enterprise | Manchester | *Montgomery
test: Segregation laws kept Black and white people apart. What were they kept apart on? | Rivers and lakes | *Buses, schools and shops | Farms and fields | Cars and bikes
test: Which sentence uses Alabama to mean a river? | The bus left Alabama this morning. | Rosa Parks sat in Alabama in 1955. | We flew to Alabama for our holiday. | *Boats travelled slowly along the Alabama.
exam: Which word in this lesson is a proper noun? | *Montgomery | boycott | seat | bus
